 61SC c  2009Ta24, 2009Ta05: {+61}Sc identified by fragmentation of {+76}Ge beam
 61SC2c  at 132 MeV/nucleon at NSCL facility using A1900 fragment separator     
 61SC3c  combined with S800 analysis beam line to form a two stage separator    
 61SC4c  system. The transmitted fragments were analyzed event-by-event in      
 61SC5c  momentum and particle identification. The nuclei of interest were      
 61SC6c  stopped in eight Si diodes which provided measurement of energy loss,  
 61SC7c  nuclear charge and total kinetic energy. The time-of-flight of each    
 61SC8c  particle that reached the detector stack was measured in four          
 61SC9c  different ways using plastic scintillators, Si detectors, and          
 61SCAc  parallel-plate avalanche counters. The simultaneous measurement of |DE 
 61SCBc  signals, the magnetic rigidity, total kinetic energy and the           
 61SCCc  time-of-flight (tof) provided unambiguous identification of the        
 61SCDc  atomic number, charge state and mass number.                           
 61SC c  1995Ri05: shell model calculations; predicted spin, binding energy,    
 61SC2c  and mass defect                                                        
 61SC c  Theory references: consult the NSR database (www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/)    
 61SC2c  for six references for structure calculations.                         
